Q. What is the purpose of Pods in Kubernetes?
Ans: A Pod is the smallest deployable unit in Kubernetes serving as a wrapper around container to enhance their funtionality and managebility,
designed to run one or more tightly coupled containers.Each Pod runs on a single worker node and can contain one or multiple containers. 
Containers within a Pod share the same network namespace, allowing them to communicate via localhost, and can access shared storage volumes.

Q. What is kubectl used for?
Ans: It provides command line for running the kubernetes and you can directly interact with kubernetes cluster.

Q. How will you debug if there is issue with pod?
Ans: We use command "kubectl describe pods <pod-name>". It will give us complete information like status of pods, ip-address, events etc. 
Also, we use command "kubectl logs <pod-name>. It will give us log information to debug. 
